511
01:02:05,645 --> 01:02:07,521
I don't know.

512
01:02:09,815 --> 01:02:13,027
My birthday's April 10, 2017.
How long do I live?

513
01:02:13,194 --> 01:02:14,987
Four years.

514
01:02:21,994 --> 01:02:23,287
More than you.

515
01:02:28,292 --> 01:02:31,003
Painful to live in fear, isn't it?

516
01:02:36,550 --> 01:02:39,845
Nothing is worse than having
an itch you can never scratch.

517
01:02:40,805 --> 01:02:42,181
I agree.

518
01:02:53,359 --> 01:02:55,319
Wake up. Time to die.

519
01:03:30,396 --> 01:03:32,273
Shakes?

520
01:03:33,899 --> 01:03:35,443
Me too.

521
01:03:39,405 --> 01:03:41,365
I get them bad.

522
01:03:46,912 --> 01:03:49,081
It's part of the business.

523
01:03:56,380 --> 01:03:57,757
I'm not in the business.

524
01:04:11,270 --> 01:04:13,481
I am the business.

525
01:05:46,407 --> 01:05:47,700
What if I go north?

526
01:05:51,912 --> 01:05:53,873
Disappear.

527
01:05:58,210 --> 01:05:59,545
Would you come after me?

528
01:06:01,714 --> 01:06:03,382
Hunt me?

529
01:06:08,137 --> 01:06:09,763
No.

530
01:06:12,433 --> 01:06:14,435
No, I wouldn't.

531
01:06:20,232 --> 01:06:21,400
I owe you one.

532
01:06:36,624 --> 01:06:38,918
But somebody would.

533
01:06:51,263 --> 01:06:53,140
Deckard...

534
01:06:55,601 --> 01:06:57,770
...you know those files on me?

535
01:06:59,104 --> 01:07:02,775
The incept date. The longevity.

536
01:07:02,942 --> 01:07:04,818
Those things.

537
01:07:06,153 --> 01:07:07,988
You saw them?

538
01:07:11,450 --> 01:07:13,160
They're...

539
01:07:13,327 --> 01:07:14,537
...classified.

540
01:07:14,703 --> 01:07:17,206
But you're a policeman.

541
01:07:17,373 --> 01:07:19,458
I...

542
01:07:19,625 --> 01:07:21,627
...didn't look at them.

543
01:07:23,671 --> 01:07:25,965
You know,
that Voight-Kampff test of yours...

544
01:07:27,007 --> 01:07:29,969
...did you ever take that test yourself?

545
01:07:41,689 --> 01:07:43,315
Deckard.

546
01:10:13,799 --> 01:10:15,509
I dreamt music.

547
01:10:20,681 --> 01:10:23,308
I didn't know if I could play.

548
01:10:24,977 --> 01:10:27,771
I remember lessons.

549
01:10:28,647 --> 01:10:32,568
I don't know if it's me
or Tyrell's niece.

550
01:10:37,156 --> 01:10:39,491
You play beautifully.

551
01:11:49,561 --> 01:11:52,064
Now you kiss me.

552
01:11:53,440 --> 01:11:54,900
I can't rely on my...

553
01:11:55,067 --> 01:11:57,736
Say, "Kiss me."

554
01:12:00,447 --> 01:12:02,366
Kiss me.

555
01:12:13,794 --> 01:12:15,754
I want you.

556
01:12:18,799 --> 01:12:20,342
I want you.

557
01:12:20,509 --> 01:12:22,094
Again.

558
01:12:22,261 --> 01:12:24,137
I want you.

559
01:12:27,307 --> 01:12:29,768
Put your hands on me.

560
01:13:51,516 --> 01:13:54,811
- What you doing?
- I'm sorry. Just peeking.

561
01:13:54,978 --> 01:13:56,480
Oh.

562
01:13:58,732 --> 01:14:01,860
- How do I look?
- You look better.

563
01:14:02,027 --> 01:14:05,072
- Just better?
- Well...

564
01:14:05,238 --> 01:14:06,531
...you look beautiful.

565
01:14:10,118 --> 01:14:11,787
Thanks.

566
01:14:18,210 --> 01:14:20,128
How old are you?

567
01:14:22,047 --> 01:14:24,091
Twenty-five.

568
01:14:24,257 --> 01:14:27,219
- What's your problem?
- Methuselah syndrome.

569
01:14:27,386 --> 01:14:28,720
What's that?

570
01:14:28,887 --> 01:14:31,890
My glands, they grow old too fast.

571
01:14:33,058 --> 01:14:37,270
- Is that why you're still on Earth?
- Yeah. I couldn't pass the medical.

572
01:14:40,273 --> 01:14:41,483
Anyway...

573
01:14:41,650 --> 01:14:43,110
...I kind of like it here.

574
01:14:45,779 --> 01:14:47,739
I like you...

575
01:14:47,906 --> 01:14:49,157
...just the way you are.

576
01:14:52,411 --> 01:14:54,204
Hi, Roy.

577
01:14:54,371 --> 01:14:55,789
Hi.

578
01:14:55,956 --> 01:14:57,666
Gosh, you...

579
01:14:57,833 --> 01:15:00,127
...really got some nice toys here.

580
01:15:00,293 --> 01:15:02,671
This is the friend I was telling you about.

581
01:15:02,838 --> 01:15:06,091
This is my savior, J.F. Sebastian.

582
01:15:06,258 --> 01:15:07,759
Sebastian.

583
01:15:08,427 --> 01:15:11,096
I like a man that stays put.

584
01:15:12,639 --> 01:15:15,976
You live here all by yourself, do you?

585
01:15:16,143 --> 01:15:17,185
Yes.

586
01:15:28,780 --> 01:15:31,116
How about some breakfast?

587
01:15:31,283 --> 01:15:33,285
I was just gonna make some.

588
01:15:33,452 --> 01:15:34,453
Excuse me.

589
01:15:41,835 --> 01:15:43,462
Well?

590
01:15:45,714 --> 01:15:46,965
Leon....

591
01:15:47,132 --> 01:15:49,134
What's going on?

592
01:15:53,472 --> 01:15:55,140
There's only two of us now.

593
01:15:57,350 --> 01:16:00,479
Then we're stupid and we'll die.

594
01:16:04,483 --> 01:16:06,693
No, we won't.

595
01:16:40,185 --> 01:16:41,186
No.

596
01:16:41,353 --> 01:16:43,897
Knight takes queen, see?

597
01:16:44,064 --> 01:16:46,024
Won't do.

598
01:16:54,366 --> 01:16:56,451
Why are you staring at us, Sebastian?

599
01:16:56,660 --> 01:16:58,036
Because...

600
01:16:58,203 --> 01:17:00,372
...you're so different.

601
01:17:01,873 --> 01:17:03,959
You're so perfect.

602
01:17:06,461 --> 01:17:08,713
Yes.

603
01:17:08,880 --> 01:17:11,049
What generation are you?

604
01:17:19,182 --> 01:17:20,392
Nexus 6.

605
01:17:20,851 --> 01:17:22,769
Ah. I knew it.

606
01:17:22,936 --> 01:17:26,231
Because I do genetic design work
for the Tyrell Corporation.

607
01:17:26,398 --> 01:17:28,567
There's some of me in you.

608
01:17:29,693 --> 01:17:31,403
Show me something.

609
01:17:31,570 --> 01:17:33,321
Like what?

610
01:17:33,488 --> 01:17:35,407
Like anything.

611
01:17:37,242 --> 01:17:42,080
We're no computers, Sebastian.
We're physical.

612
01:17:43,832 --> 01:17:46,084
I think, Sebastian...

613
01:17:46,251 --> 01:17:48,670
...therefore, I am.

614
01:17:48,837 --> 01:17:52,132
Very good, Pris. Now show him why.

615
01:18:19,034 --> 01:18:20,785
We've got a lot in common.

616
01:18:20,952 --> 01:18:23,205
- What do you mean?
- Similar problems.

617
01:18:23,371 --> 01:18:26,166
Accelerated decrepitude.

618
01:18:28,043 --> 01:18:30,837
I don't know much
about biomechanics, Roy. I wish I did.

619
01:18:32,964 --> 01:18:35,467
If we don't find help soon...

620
01:18:35,634 --> 01:18:38,511
...Pris hasn't got long to live.

621
01:18:38,678 --> 01:18:40,472
We can't allow that.

622
01:18:42,641 --> 01:18:45,852
- Is he good?
- Who?

623
01:18:46,019 --> 01:18:49,397
- Your opponent.
- Oh, Dr. Tyrell?

624
01:18:49,564 --> 01:18:53,026
I've only beaten him once in chess.
He's a genius.

625
01:18:55,320 --> 01:18:56,321
He designed you.

626
01:18:58,782 --> 01:19:01,326
Maybe he could help.

627
01:19:01,493 --> 01:19:04,037
I'd be happy to mention it to him.

628
01:19:06,164 --> 01:19:09,668
Better if I talk to him in person.

629
01:19:12,754 --> 01:19:17,842
But I understand
he's a sort of hard man to get to.

630
01:19:18,009 --> 01:19:19,928
Yes.

631
01:19:20,095 --> 01:19:21,721
Very.

632
01:19:24,683 --> 01:19:27,060
Will you help us?

633
01:19:27,811 --> 01:19:29,104
I can't.

634
01:19:29,312 --> 01:19:31,273
We need you, Sebastian.

635
01:19:31,439 --> 01:19:34,359
You're our best and only friend.

636
01:19:47,372 --> 01:19:49,833
We're so happy you found us.

637
01:19:51,626 --> 01:19:53,712
I don't think
there's another human being...

638
01:19:53,878 --> 01:19:56,214
...in the whole world
who would've helped us.

639
01:20:45,138 --> 01:20:49,642
66,000 Prosser & Ankovich. Hm.

640
01:20:49,934 --> 01:20:51,353
Trade.

641
01:20:51,519 --> 01:20:54,272
- Trade at two...
<i>- Blue entry.</i>

642
01:20:55,273 --> 01:20:58,651
<i>A Mr. J.F. Sebastian.</i>

643
01:20:58,818 --> 01:21:02,947
<i>16417.</i>

644
01:21:03,698 --> 01:21:05,450
<i>At this hour?</i>

645
01:21:05,617 --> 01:21:08,787
<i>What can I do for you, Sebastian?</i>

646
01:21:11,956 --> 01:21:13,458
Queen to bishop six. Check.

647
01:21:19,047 --> 01:21:21,216
Nonsense.

648
01:21:21,424 --> 01:21:23,635
Just a moment.

649
01:21:26,554 --> 01:21:31,309
Queen to bishop six, ridiculous.

650
01:21:36,940 --> 01:21:38,650
Queen...

651
01:21:40,318 --> 01:21:42,320
...bishop six.

652
01:21:43,321 --> 01:21:44,322
Hm.

653
01:21:47,450 --> 01:21:49,828
<i>Knight...</i>

654
01:21:49,994 --> 01:21:52,205
<i>...takes queen.</i>

655
01:21:59,003 --> 01:22:01,423
What's on your mind, Sebastian?

656
01:22:01,589 --> 01:22:03,049
What are you thinking about?

657
01:22:04,676 --> 01:22:06,886
Bishop to king seven.

658
01:22:07,053 --> 01:22:09,097
Checkmate.

659
01:22:09,264 --> 01:22:11,349
Bishop to king seven.
Checkmate, I think.

660
01:22:13,184 --> 01:22:16,396
Got a brainstorm, huh, Sebastian?

661
01:22:16,563 --> 01:22:19,524
Milk and cookies
kept you awake, huh?

662
01:22:19,691 --> 01:22:21,860
<i>Let's discuss this.</i>

663
01:22:22,026 --> 01:22:24,028
<i>You better come up, Sebastian.</i>

664
01:22:41,629 --> 01:22:43,590
Mr. Tyrell?

665
01:22:45,383 --> 01:22:47,051
I....

666
01:22:47,218 --> 01:22:49,137
I brought a friend.

667
01:22:55,393 --> 01:22:59,397
I'm surprised
you didn't come here sooner.

668
01:23:06,070 --> 01:23:09,240
It's not an easy thing
to meet your maker.

669
01:23:09,949 --> 01:23:12,911
And what can he do for you?

670
01:23:13,620 --> 01:23:17,123
Can the maker repair what he makes?

671
01:23:17,290 --> 01:23:20,627
Would you like to be modified?

672
01:23:20,793 --> 01:23:22,754
Stay here.

673
01:23:27,926 --> 01:23:31,304
Had in mind something
a little more radical.

674
01:23:31,930 --> 01:23:33,932
What...?

675
01:23:34,098 --> 01:23:36,601
What seems to be the problem?

676
01:23:36,935 --> 01:23:39,562
- Death.
- Death.

677
01:23:40,188 --> 01:23:43,274
Well, I'm afraid that's
a little out of my jurisdiction. You...

678
01:23:43,441 --> 01:23:46,444
I want more life...

679
01:23:46,611 --> 01:23:47,862
...father.

680
01:23:52,784 --> 01:23:54,953
The facts of life.

681
01:23:56,329 --> 01:23:59,123
To make an alteration in the...

682
01:23:59,290 --> 01:24:01,709
...evolvement of
an organic life system is fatal.

683
01:24:01,876 --> 01:24:05,463
A coding sequence cannot be revised
once it's been established.

684
01:24:05,630 --> 01:24:06,631
Why not?

685
01:24:06,798 --> 01:24:08,841
Because by the second day
of incubation...

686
01:24:09,008 --> 01:24:13,513
...any cells that have undergone
reversion mutations...

687
01:24:13,680 --> 01:24:17,976
...give rise to revertant colonies
like rats leaving a sinking ship.

688
01:24:18,142 --> 01:24:19,894
Then the ship sinks.

689
01:24:20,103 --> 01:24:23,648
What about EMS recombination?

690
01:24:23,815 --> 01:24:25,316
We've already tried it.

691
01:24:25,483 --> 01:24:29,821
Ethyl methane sulfonate is an
alkylating agent and a potent mutagen.

692
01:24:29,988 --> 01:24:34,075
It created a virus so lethal...

693
01:24:34,242 --> 01:24:36,411
...the subject was dead
before he left the table.

694
01:24:36,619 --> 01:24:39,664
Then a repressor protein
that blocks the operating cells.

695
01:24:39,831 --> 01:24:43,835
Wouldn't obstruct replication, but it
does give rise to an error in replication.

696
01:24:44,002 --> 01:24:48,673
So that the newly formed DNA strand
carries a mutation...

697
01:24:48,840 --> 01:24:51,718
...and you've got a virus again.

698
01:24:51,884 --> 01:24:56,347
But this, all of this, is...

699
01:24:56,514 --> 01:24:58,099
...academic.

700
01:24:58,266 --> 01:25:00,768
You were made
as well as we could make you.

701
01:25:00,935 --> 01:25:02,687
But not to last.

702
01:25:03,521 --> 01:25:06,691
The light that burns twice as bright
burns half as long.

703
01:25:06,858 --> 01:25:11,070
And you have burned
so very, very brightly, Roy.

704
01:25:11,696 --> 01:25:13,448
Look at you.

705
01:25:13,656 --> 01:25:16,200
You're the prodigal son.

706
01:25:16,367 --> 01:25:19,871
You're quite a prize.

707
01:25:25,543 --> 01:25:27,045
I've done...

708
01:25:27,211 --> 01:25:28,880
...questionable things.

709
01:25:29,047 --> 01:25:30,923
Also extraordinary things.

710
01:25:31,549 --> 01:25:33,926
Revel in your time.

711
01:25:37,889 --> 01:25:42,393
Nothing the god of biomechanics
wouldn't let you in heaven for.

712
01:26:34,612 --> 01:26:37,365
Sorry, Sebastian.

713
01:26:37,740 --> 01:26:40,743
Come. Come.

714
01:27:27,165 --> 01:27:29,500
<i>Body identified with Tyrell...</i>

715
01:27:29,667 --> 01:27:32,003
<i>...is a 25-year-old male Caucasian.</i>

716
01:27:32,170 --> 01:27:35,006
<i>Name: Sebastian, J.F. Sebastian.</i>

717
01:27:35,173 --> 01:27:40,011
<i>Address: Bradbury Apartments,
Ninth Sector, NF46751.</i>

718
01:27:40,178 --> 01:27:41,846
<i>I want you to go down there and...</i>

719
01:27:45,850 --> 01:27:48,895
<i>This sector's closed to
ground traffic. What are you doing here?</i>

720
01:27:49,061 --> 01:27:52,732
- I'm working. What are you doing?
<i>- Arresting you, that's what I'm doing.</i>

721
01:27:52,899 --> 01:27:57,612
I'm Deckard, Blade Runner.
26354. I'm filed and monitored.

722
01:27:57,820 --> 01:27:59,030
<i>Hold on. Checking.</i>

723
01:28:03,201 --> 01:28:06,913
<i>Okay. Checked and cleared.
Have a better one.</i>

724
01:28:17,465 --> 01:28:19,467
<i>- Hello.</i>
- Hi. Is J.F. there?

725
01:28:19,634 --> 01:28:23,054
<i>- Who is it?</i>
- This is Eddie, old friend of J.F.'s.

726
01:28:26,933 --> 01:28:28,643
That's no way to treat a friend.

727
01:31:27,238 --> 01:31:29,323
Home again, home again, jiggidy-jig.

728
01:31:30,449 --> 01:31:33,411
Good evening, J.F.

729
01:31:43,587 --> 01:31:45,423
<i>Tea?</i>

730
01:31:46,757 --> 01:31:48,592
<i>More tea?</i>

731
01:31:49,635 --> 01:31:50,678
<i>Tea?</i>

732
01:32:00,229 --> 01:32:02,106
<i>More tea?</i>

733
01:32:04,358 --> 01:32:06,110
<i>Tea?</i>

734
01:32:07,695 --> 01:32:09,613
<i>More tea?</i>

735
01:32:11,198 --> 01:32:13,159
<i>More tea?</i>

736
01:32:25,588 --> 01:32:27,465
<i>More tea?</i>

737
01:35:33,067 --> 01:35:36,820
Not very sporting to fire
on an unarmed opponent.

738
01:35:38,405 --> 01:35:41,784
I thought you were
supposed to be good.

739
01:35:43,077 --> 01:35:45,746
Aren't you the good man?

740
01:35:50,584 --> 01:35:54,255
Come on, Deckard.

741
01:35:55,422 --> 01:35:57,299
Show me...

742
01:35:58,133 --> 01:36:00,261
...what you're made of.

743
01:36:12,273 --> 01:36:14,149
Proud of yourself, little man?

744
01:36:22,074 --> 01:36:25,077
- This is for Zhora.
- Ah!

745
01:36:25,452 --> 01:36:28,122
- This is for Pris.
- Ah!

746
01:36:33,961 --> 01:36:35,462
Come on, Deckard.

747
01:36:36,005 --> 01:36:39,216
I'm right here,
but you've gotta shoot straight.

748
01:36:40,551 --> 01:36:42,970
Straight doesn't seem
to be good enough!

749
01:36:43,137 --> 01:36:44,179
Now it's my turn.

750
01:36:46,098 --> 01:36:49,810
I'm gonna give you a few seconds
before I come.

751
01:36:50,519 --> 01:36:51,812
One.

752
01:36:51,979 --> 01:36:54,189
Two.

753
01:37:06,160 --> 01:37:07,995
Three.

754
01:37:08,162 --> 01:37:10,122
Four.

755
01:37:22,384 --> 01:37:24,053
Pris.

756
01:38:09,139 --> 01:38:11,183
Ah!

757
01:38:34,623 --> 01:38:39,002
I'm coming.

758
01:38:39,211 --> 01:38:40,963
Deckard!

759
01:38:43,424 --> 01:38:44,716
<i>Four, five</i>

760
01:38:47,928 --> 01:38:51,098
<i>How to stay alive?</i>

761
01:39:13,996 --> 01:39:15,622
I can see you!

762
01:39:41,482 --> 01:39:43,734
Not yet!

763
01:39:43,901 --> 01:39:44,985
Not....

764
01:40:12,054 --> 01:40:13,096
Ah!

765
01:40:17,726 --> 01:40:19,520
Five.

766
01:40:22,731 --> 01:40:24,274
Five.

767
01:40:28,445 --> 01:40:29,613
Yes.

768
01:40:37,538 --> 01:40:39,039
You better get it up.

769
01:40:39,706 --> 01:40:41,208
Or I'm gonna have to kill you.

770
01:40:42,251 --> 01:40:44,545
Unless you're alive, you can't play.

771
01:40:44,711 --> 01:40:46,672
And if you don't play....

772
01:40:56,265 --> 01:40:58,475
<i>Six, seven</i>

773
01:40:58,684 --> 01:41:00,561
<i>Go to hell or go to heaven</i>

774
01:41:08,068 --> 01:41:09,736
Good, that's the spirit!

775
01:41:51,111 --> 01:41:53,280
That hurt.

776
01:41:56,533 --> 01:41:58,660
That was irrational of you.

777
01:42:00,621 --> 01:42:01,955
Not to mention...

778
01:42:02,623 --> 01:42:04,958
...unsportsmanlike.

779
01:42:09,004 --> 01:42:11,006
Where are you going?

780
01:45:15,482 --> 01:45:19,361
Quite an experience to live in fear,
isn't it?

781
01:45:21,071 --> 01:45:24,157
That's what it is to be a slave.

782
01:46:23,049 --> 01:46:24,301
I've...

783
01:46:24,467 --> 01:46:29,556
...seen things
you people wouldn't believe.

784
01:46:31,099 --> 01:46:36,271
Attack ships on fire
off the shoulder of Orion.

785
01:46:38,231 --> 01:46:40,567
I watched C-beams...

786
01:46:40,734 --> 01:46:44,404
...glitter in the dark
near the Tannhäuser Gate.

787
01:46:48,575 --> 01:46:50,619
All those...

788
01:46:50,785 --> 01:46:53,830
...moments will be lost...

789
01:46:53,997 --> 01:46:56,249
...in time...

790
01:46:57,792 --> 01:47:00,086
...like...

791
01:47:00,253 --> 01:47:01,963
...tears...

792
01:47:03,423 --> 01:47:05,634
...in rain.

793
01:47:09,262 --> 01:47:11,806
Time to die.

794
01:48:17,747 --> 01:48:20,667
You've done a man's job, sir.

795
01:48:26,339 --> 01:48:28,717
I guess you're through, huh?

796
01:48:30,760 --> 01:48:32,554
Finished.

797
01:48:54,576 --> 01:48:57,579
It's too bad she won't live.

798
01:48:58,580 --> 01:49:01,082
But then again, who does?

799
01:49:34,741 --> 01:49:36,576
Rachael?

800
01:49:44,292 --> 01:49:46,044
Rachael?

801
01:49:59,933 --> 01:50:01,476
Rachael?

802
01:51:08,209 --> 01:51:10,003
Do you love me?

803
01:51:11,171 --> 01:51:12,881
I love you.

804
01:51:13,756 --> 01:51:15,675
Do you trust me?

805
01:51:16,843 --> 01:51:18,845
I trust you.

806
01:51:28,354 --> 01:51:29,898
Rachael?

807
01:52:09,479 --> 01:52:12,398
<i>It's too bad she won't live.</i>

808
01:52:12,565 --> 01:52:15,193
<i>But then again, who does?</i>

